# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normalize line endings so a Windows/Linux CI runner never sees phantom diffs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# project.pbxproj is Xcode's project database. It is technically text, but it
# is machine-generated and merges catastrophically.
#
# `merge=union` tells git: when both sides added lines, keep BOTH instead of
# emitting conflict markers. This resolves the overwhelmingly common case --
# two branches each added new files -- automatically and correctly.
#
# It is not magic: if two branches edit the SAME build setting, union merge
# keeps both lines and Xcode will complain. That is your signal to open the
# project and fix it by hand. Always open Xcode after a pbxproj merge.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pbxproj merge=union linguist-generated=true
*.pbxproj -diff

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets: never try to diff or merge these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.m4a    binary
*.wav    binary
*.aiff   binary
*.mp3    binary
*.mlmodel   binary
*.mlmodelc  binary
*.mlpackage binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep generated/vendored files out of GitHub's language stats and out of
# "Files changed" by default in PRs, so reviewers see real code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcscheme  linguist-generated=true
Package.resolved linguist-generated=true
